  "body": "What happens: `edit_operation` with `stepdown: -3` on a 2D Pocket returns \"operation parameters are not usable for a 2D Pocket operation\". The refusal does not say which field or why, so an agent (or a person using the script API) cannot correct the call. Found in the local-model MCP benchmark of 2026-11-22.\n\nExpected: the refusal names the field and the rule, for example \"stepdown must be greater than 0 (got -3)\".\n\nDone means: parameter refusals from edit_operation and add_operation name the offending field and its limit; a test pins the stepdown case.\n",
